## Progress on `cache_coherency` — unlink_visibility FIXED

**Build `286311EE` (KEEP)** — `unlink_visibility` now PASSES (rc=0, 36s, 4 nodes), the last failing subtest of the only remaining ship-gate criterion.

### Root cause (proven, RULE-4 instrument + RULE-5 Gemini reconcile)
The acquire-side `mxfs_dir_drain_evict_data_blocks` gated its dir-block eviction on `!dirty && !in_ail && !delwri`. That **`!in_ail` skip was the lost-update source**: during the concurrent create/delete storm, a node acquiring dir EX kept its own in-AIL cached dir block (committed but log-tail-pending) and RMW'd that **stale base**, durably dropping a peer's just-committed dirents. Signature: a node's own `rm` returning ENOENT on a *contiguous range of files it created* (`node3_file2..19`), no I/O error — a peer had clobbered them; other nodes then saw them as survivors.

### The fix
Evict (clear `XBF_DONE` only — **not** `xfs_buf_stale`) **all non-pinned** dir blocks; only PINNED stays a hard skip. Safe now because **publish-before-notify** (sess97) fences every committed dir change to the LUN before any peer is told, so a plain cold-read reliably sees the durable image (resolving the long-standing sess96/99-vs-sess69 "is transport coherent" contradiction — it is, post-publish).

### Decisive instrument
P-DIRWR write-trace + **synchronizing the 4 nodes' wall clocks** (they drift ~1.5s/node, which had been silently breaking every prior cross-node timeline merge) → proved the delete-phase writes are monotonic (no delete clobber), pointing to a create-phase acquire-stale-base, confirmed by the rm-ENOENT signature.

### Criteria NOT yet met — marker NOT written
**Next session**: clean reboot + `reset4.sh 4` (deploys `286311EE`), re-verify `rename_visibility` stays PASS + `cross_visibility` + `cross_write_read` (the drain_evict change could affect them), then full `cache_coherency.sh` must be 4/4, then `verify_ship.sh` end-to-end. The read-path twin `mxfs_dir_evict_data_blocks` (L379) still has the old `!in_ail` skip — apply the same in-AIL-safe evict there if a visibility residual appears. Watch the intermittent bnobt double-free shutdown (separate blocker). Full detail saved to memory `sess101_lessons`.

